  "completed_actions": [
    "Read migration goal and prior plan/module documents",
    "Inspected origin/main, repository permissions and existing exact-SHA CI",
    "Created provisional full legacy requirement mapping and source inventory",
    "Committed R0.1 locally as b1dbd9f; actual push failed HTTP 403; migration CI remains unrun",
    "All five exact-SHA R0.1 workflows passed, including all three-OS baseline jobs; access blocker resolved",
    "Reviewed 196 legacy requirements and 15 Rust migration-specific requirements; mapped all 231 inventoried files to Rust responsibilities.",
    "Reviewed all 196 inherited requirements and 15 migration-specific requirements; reconciled 231 source, test, fixture and tooling mappings.",
    "R0.2 inventory and all four existing platform CI workflows passed on exact SHA d79e500d18fe87c23c7617bdc5fcdd9c10ef7c74; exact-SHA jobs recorded in evidence/r0.2-ci.json.",
    "Added the minimal Cargo workspace, read-only vault session, native eframe shell, platform/plugin interfaces, shared test helper, layering xtask and three-OS Rust workflow locally; all executable validation remains pending GitHub Actions.",
    "GitHub Rust CI identified formatting-only differences and the eframe 0.36 App::ui API; corrected both from CI output and retrieved Cargo.lock from exact-SHA run 37669853135 (artifact digest e12ecff53e0b4613a3077731c3862ff674f7db738d7dc8aa392a9dde20fd128b). Fresh CI is pending for the correction.",
    "R1.1 native workspace, Cargo.lock, minimal eframe shell and layering gate passed the exact-SHA Rust GitHub Actions matrix on Linux, macOS and Windows; all legacy quality/package/plugin workflows also passed. Evidence: evidence/r1.1-ci.json; Linux preview artifact recorded there.",
    "Reconciled the updated goal documentation requirement as MIG-016 and added RM-08; R0.2 historical mapping count remains 211 and current requirements count is 212.",
    "Started R1.2 with a Wry 0.57.0 system-WebView feasibility probe for unchanged PC05 Advanced Tables and PC08 Style Settings bundles; runtime reports retain Pending/non-certifying status and include bundle/manifest/stylesheet hashes, WebView identity, DOM/editor metrics and capability denials.",
    "Hardened the Wry probe boundary after source review: navigation is limited to the exact localhost probe document, custom protocol assets reject unexpected hosts, frame ancestors are denied, and browser autofill is disabled where supported. No local executable validation was run.",
    "GitHub Actions lockfile resolver run 37678837444 passed for source ce6097ab2625bddb34905b85a47a35b7e7fa602e; its Cargo.lock artifact was retrieved and hashed, and the temporary resolver workflow was removed. This run generated dependency metadata only; implementation validation remains pending.",
    "Rust CI 37679025109 reported Linux rustfmt differences and a Wry navigation callback signature mismatch on macOS/Windows; no plugin probe ran. Corrected from GitHub output. The following exact-SHA inventory and quality matrices passed on e264e9f65da1cad16e23b55cec3a510379ebd072; its Rust CI is pending.",
    "Rust CI source SHA 21928f8658ef948853d351da13734b1523be81d5 passed Linux format, tests, Clippy, layering and release build, then failed before WebView creation in winit's X11 XKB event-loop initialization. Artifact 11509255875 records pinned PC05/PC08 integrity passing but zero plugins executed. Added Ubuntu's libxkbcommon-x11-0 runtime dependency to CI and documented the environment finding; rerun on exact source SHA before promoting feasibility.",
    "On source SHA 21928f8658ef948853d351da13734b1523be81d5 the macOS and Windows Wry probes launched and passed capability denials, but both verified unchanged bundles failed on an Obsidian Modal superclass missing from the test shim. Reports are summarized in evidence/r1.2-plugin-runtime-desktop-21928f8.json. Static inspection of the SHA-verified bundle assets confirmed Modal subclasses; the probe now adds a minimal Modal DOM/API and uses string DOM helper arguments as CSS classes.",
    "Exact-SHA inventory run 37682834615 identified a missing next_action JSON key in the R1.2 state entry; corrected from the GitHub parser diagnostic. Quality run 37682834698 passed macOS/Windows but Ubuntu's Electron vault round-trip audit failed before retrieval; the next exact-SHA matrix must record a fresh result.",
    "The XKB/X11 Linux dependency update on source SHA ee263c65c5fc303633b5611bf30ad9b3d5a984e3 allowed the Linux Wry/WebKitGTK probe to start and pass its direct capability checks; both plugins then reached the missing Modal shim. Evidence: evidence/r1.2-linux-xkb-runtime-ee263c6.json. The Modal/DOM fix is in the subsequent exact-SHA Rust run.",
    "Exact-SHA inventory, quality, desktop, renderer and loaded-plugin workflows passed on d96d781b21ae17386dda1403fa5813a31f04fb8f. Rust CI run 37683082486 exposed a Windows vault test failure from likely concurrent temporary-directory name collisions; the test helper now uses process-scoped atomic directory allocation. Linux and macOS Rust jobs were still running when this state was updated.",
    "The d96d781 macOS Rust job built the preview, passed tests/Clippy/layer checks and ran the Wry probe. Artifact 11509358621 showed PC05 had not registered commands because the fixture did not wait for its asyncOnload work; PC08 required Obsidian's activeWindow alias. Recorded in evidence/r1.2-plugin-runtime-macos-d96d781.json and corrected in the probe fixture.",
    "Rust CI run 37684304691 reported one rustfmt-only difference in the temporary vault helper on Linux; the exact CI-requested layout is applied. On macOS and Windows, workspace tests, Clippy, layering and native preview builds passed, while unchanged PC05/PC08 probes exposed the asynchronous-startup and activeWindow fixture gaps. Inventory, quality, desktop, renderer and loaded-plugin workflows passed on ec27f5aa156d494a444b779b27bdfe300a39ffca. Exact reports and digests are in evidence/r1.2-plugin-runtime-desktop-ec27f5a.json."
  ],
